WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
In June 2022, US consumer
prices were up 9.1

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.800
percent from a year earlier.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.260
The Fed responded with its main tool:

4
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.820
the target for the federal funds rate.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.670
The target range climbed
from 0 to 0.25 percent,

6
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:20.780
all the way up to 5.25 to 5.50 percent.

7
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.600
But how can one interest rate,

8
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.510
set by a handful of people,

9
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.730
slow down inflation
across a whole country?

10
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.270
In this mission, you'll
trace how the Fed's moves

11
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:34.470
travel through the money market
to real GDP and the price level.

12
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.090
Then you'll take control in a graph lab:

13
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:40.390
set the policy rate, and
watch the output gap.

14
00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.840
Your mission: explain how a
single rate decision reaches

15
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.950
prices across the whole economy.
